# Mobile (`mobile/`)

Relevant role specs: `.claude/agents/mobile-architect.md`, `.claude/agents/mobile-engineer.md`.
Architecture foundation doc: `docs/features/003-mobile-app-foundation/architecture.md` — read
this before adding any new screen or changing navigation/auth structure.

## Non-negotiable patterns already established

- **Never talk to Supabase or MongoDB directly from the app.** Every request goes through the
  backend's `/api/v1/*` contract. The base URL is `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` (see
  `mobile/.env`, `src/api/config.ts`) — a host, not a secret, fine to inline at build time.
- **Token handling**: refresh token → `expo-secure-store`. Access token → in-memory only,
  never persisted. Auto-refresh on 401 via `src/api/client.ts`.
- **Device binding (FR-20)**: a locally-generated `deviceId` (`src/auth/device.ts`,
  `getOrCreateDeviceId()`) is sent on **both** login and session-refresh calls — this exact
  omission on refresh was a real, already-fixed bug (api-design.md v1.1.0 §11 Amendment C).
  Reuse that one function; don't create a second device-identity mechanism.
- **API types are generated, not hand-written**: `mobile/openapi/identity-service.yaml` is
  copied from the backend's `api-design.md` OpenAPI block; `src/api/generated/*.ts` is
  produced via `npm run generate:api-types`. If the backend contract has a new amendment,
  update the yaml first, then regenerate — don't hand-edit the generated file, and don't
  assume the generator script's output is fresh without checking (it silently produced a
  stale file once when invoked via a different path than expected).
- **Design system**: `src/theme/primitives/*` is an explicitly **temporary** bridge from the
  web design system (`src/components/*` at repo root) — every file in it is headed with a
  "temporary, do not extend independently" note. Don't add new primitives here without
  checking whether `design-system-manager`'s planned RN port has landed first. Current
  inventory includes `FormField`, `SelectChipGroup`, and (new) `Toggle`
  (`mobile/src/theme/primitives/Toggle.tsx`, used by `NotificationPreferencesScreen`) — reuse
  before adding another.
- **Policy/asset screens are real, not placeholders** — this note is stale-corrected: Feature
  004's customer API shipped and `PolicyListScreen`, `CreatePolicyScreen`, `AssetListScreen`,
  `RegisterAssetScreen`, and their detail routes are wired to the live backend. Check
  `HANDOFF.md`'s "What actually exists" section before assuming any given mobile screen is a
  stub — several that once were no longer are (notifications preferences is the latest).
